#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:3 of
msgid ""
"Caches serialized Arrow batches and flushes them as a single Arrow IPC "
"stream body via :meth:`stub.write_table`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:10 of
msgid "Write session ID."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:12 of
msgid "Write stream ID (use different IDs for parallel writers)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:14 of
msgid "Write stream version."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:18 of
msgid "Server routing token for session affinity."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter:20 of
msgid "Arrow IPC compression for write batches."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.build_blob_write_item:1
#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.build_blob_write_item:1 of
msgid "Build a :class:`BlobWriteItem` from writer-resolved state."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.build_blob_write_item:3 of
msgid ""
"``column_name`` is resolved to the server-assigned column ID via "
":meth:`WriteSchema.find_all_blob_column_ids` (same dot-path keys). When "
"omitted, the sole top-level pure-BLOB column is auto-selected (raises if "
"the schema has multiple BLOB columns or any nested BLOB column).  "
"``partition_spec`` accepts the same types as "
":class:`~odps.types.PartitionSpec` (str, dict, or PartitionSpec). "
"``api_version`` is stamped from the writer so v3-only fields "
"(``custom_file_name``) are gated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.close:1 of
msgid "Flush remaining data, then closeWriteStream."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.close:3 of
msgid ""
"Skips closeWriteStream when (a) streaming with session_id == \"default\" "
"OR (b) stream_id == \"default\"; otherwise closes the stream."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.close:6 of
msgid ""
"The async-flush executor is always shut down (even if flush or "
"closeWriteStream raises) so its worker thread is joined."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush:1 of
msgid "Send all cached batches as one Arrow IPC stream body."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush:3 of
msgid ""
"If an async flush is in flight, awaits and surfaces its exception first, "
"then sync-flushes the remaining buffer."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush_async:1 of
msgid "Async flush using a ThreadPoolExecutor + Semaphore for backpressure."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush_async:3 of
msgid ""
"Captures all buffer state (including ``_cached_record_batches`` needed "
"for compressed writes), submits the flush to a background worker, and "
"retains the Future in a pending deque so failures surface from the next "
"``write_batch`` / ``flush`` / ``close``.  The semaphore provides real "
"backpressure: when ``max_pending_buffers`` flushes are in flight the next"
" ``flush_async`` blocks until one completes."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush_async:10 of
msgid ""
"Every submitted Future is tracked in ``_pending_futures`` (not a single "
"scalar) so that ``flush()``, ``close()``, and ``set_row_offset()`` await "
"*all* pending uploads, and a failure in one buffer is not erased by a "
"success in another."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.flush_async:15 of
msgid ""
"On async failure the captured rows are restored to the live cache "
"(appended after any live data to preserve submission order) so the caller"
" can retry.  Returns the Future (a completed Future when there is nothing"
" to flush) so callers can always ``.result()`` it."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_as_record_writer:1 of
msgid "Return a record-oriented writer wrapping this writer."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_as_record_writer:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns :class:`DeltaTableRecordWriter` if an ``__operation`` column is "
"found in either ``system_columns`` or ``columns``; otherwise "
":class:`AppendTableRecordWriter`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_as_record_writer:7 of
msgid ""
"On a plain :class:`TableArrowWriter`, BLOB cells must already contain "
"reference bytes.  On a :class:`TableArrowBlobUploadWriter`, raw ``bytes``"
" / file-like values are auto-uploaded and replaced with references."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_as_record_writer:12 of
msgid "rows per Arrow batch flush."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_as_record_writer:13 of
msgid "max blobs per batch upload."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.get_row_offset:1 of
msgid "In EO mode, fetch the latest server-side RowOffset; else return local."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.set_row_offset:1 of
msgid "Flush cached data with current offset, then update (EO mode only)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.set_row_offset:3 of
msgid ""
"Awaits any in-flight async flush first so the detached flush cannot race "
"with the offset change and write rows at the wrong position."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_batch:1 of
msgid "Serialize a batch to Arrow IPC bytes and cache it."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_batch:3 of
msgid ""
"``batch`` may be a :class:`pa.Table` or :class:`pa.RecordBatch`. Auto-"
"flushes at ``buffer_size``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_batch:6 of
msgid ""
"BLOB column values are sent inline as-is.  To auto-upload raw ``bytes`` "
"and replace them with references, use :class:`TableArrowBlobUploadWriter`"
" via ``auto_upload_blobs=True``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_batch:1 of
msgid "Batch blob upload.  Returns :class:`WriteBlobResponse`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_batch:3 of
msgid ""
"Streams frames to the server via chunked transfer-encoding — the full "
"batch body is never materialized."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_stream:1 of
msgid "Streaming single blob upload with MD5 verification."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_stream:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`BlobStreamWriter` that streams data to the server via "
"chunked transfer-encoding — the full blob is never materialized."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_stream:6 of
msgid ""
"``column_name`` is the dot-path name (a key of "
":meth:`WriteSchema.find_all_blob_column_ids`) resolved to the server-"
"assigned column ID internally.  When omitted, the sole top-level pure-"
"BLOB column is auto-selected (raises if the schema has multiple BLOB "
"columns or any nested BLOB column)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowWriter.write_blob_stream:12 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``partition_spec`` accepts the same types as "
":class:`~odps.types.PartitionSpec` (str, dict, or PartitionSpec "
"instance), e.g. ``\"pt=20230101\"`` or ``{\"pt\": \"20230101\"}``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:1 of
msgid "Arrow writer that auto-uploads BLOB cells and replaces with references."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:3 of
msgid ""
"Subclass of :class:`TableArrowWriter`.  ``write_batch`` is overridden to "
"batch-upload raw ``bytes`` / file-like BLOB cells via "
"``table_batch_write_blob`` and replace them with reference bytes before "
"forwarding to ``super().write_batch``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:8 of
msgid ""
"Use this writer when you want inline BLOB content uploaded automatically "
"— create it via ``auto_upload_blobs=True`` on :meth:`TableWriteSession."
"open_arrow_writer`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:12
#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:13 of
msgid "Forwarded to :class:`TableArrowWriter`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:14 of
msgid "Checksum algorithm for blob uploads."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:16 of
msgid "Session-level default MIME type for blobs."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:18 of
msgid "Session-level default custom file name (API v3 only)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter:20 of
msgid ""
"``callback(row_index, column_name, blob_data) -> (mime_type, "
"custom_file_name) | None`` invoked once per inline BLOB cell."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter.write_batch:1 of
msgid "Override: batch-upload BLOB cells, replace with refs, then super()."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.writer.TableArrowBlobUploadWriter.write_batch:3 of
msgid ""
"A ``pa.Table`` may contain multiple record-batch chunks; each chunk is "
"processed independently."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter:1 of
msgid "Row-oriented writer wrapping :class:`TableArrowWriter`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter:3 of
msgid ""
"Converts Record -> Arrow batches.  When the underlying writer has "
"``auto_upload_blobs=True``, BLOB columns are intercepted: file-like "
"objects and raw ``bytes``/``bytearray`` are batch-uploaded by the record "
"writer itself and replaced with references pass through unchanged.  When "
"``auto_upload_blobs=False``, BLOB cells must already contain reference "
"bytes."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter.close:1 of
msgid "Flush remaining records, then close the underlying writer."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter.flush:1 of
msgid "Flush buffered records, then flush the underlying writer."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter.write:1 of
msgid "Write a single record."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter.write:3 of
msgid ""
"Accepts ``odps.types.Record``, ``list``, or ``tuple``.  BLOB columns may "
"contain: ``bytes``/``bytearray`` (batch-uploaded by the record writer), "
"file-like (streamed in chunks, never fully materialized), ``str`` (blob "
"reference, passed through), ``None`` (null)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.AppendTableRecordWriter.write:9 of
msgid ""
"Auto-flushes when ``row_count >= row_count_per_batch`` or when the "
"accumulated blob file count >= ``blob_batch_file_num``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.DeltaTableRecordWriter:1 of
msgid "Record writer for Delta Tables (primary key tables)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.DeltaTableRecordWriter:3 of
msgid ""
"``write()`` stamps ``__operation='U'`` (UPSERT) and ``delete()`` stamps "
"``__operation='D'`` (DELETE) on each record.  Both operations can be "
"freely interleaved on a single writer instance."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.DeltaTableRecordWriter.delete:1 of
msgid "Write a record as a DELETE (``__operation='D'``)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.write.record_writer.DeltaTableRecordWriter.write:1 of
msgid "Write a record as an UPSERT (``__operation='U'``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api-maxstorage.rst:58
msgid "Blob I/O"
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager:1 of
msgid "Standalone blob read/write manager."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager:3 of
msgid ""
"Constructed from a :class:`MaxStorageClient`; reuses its "
":class:`StorageStub` for all HTTP operations."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager:6 of
msgid "The parent client."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager:8 of
msgid ""
"Table identifier — required for write operations (``write_blob_stream``, "
"``write_blob_batch``)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.build_blob_write_item:3 of
msgid ""
"``column_name`` is resolved to the server-assigned column ID via the "
"write schema.  When omitted, the sole top-level pure-BLOB column is auto-"
"selected (raises if the schema has multiple BLOB columns or any nested "
"BLOB column).  ``partition_spec`` accepts the same types as "
":class:`~odps.types.PartitionSpec`. ``api_version`` is stamped from the "
"client so v3-only fields are gated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blob:1 of
msgid "Download a single blob and return a :class:`io.BytesIO` over its data."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blob:3 of
msgid ""
"Delegates to :meth:`read_blobs` with a single-element reference list. The"
" server returns a raw unframed stream for single-ref requests, so no "
"frame headers are parsed.  Compression follows the same pattern as "
":meth:`read_blobs`: ``compress_option`` (default ``None`` = uncompressed)"
" or the shorthand ``compress_algo``.  The reference must be UTF-8 "
"decodable."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blobs:1 of
msgid "Download blobs by their references."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blobs:3 of
msgid "The server's response framing depends on the number of references:"
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blobs:5 of
msgid ""
"**Single reference**: the server returns raw unframed blob bytes (no "
"``[HeaderLen][Header][DataLen][Data]`` frames).  The entire decompressed "
"payload is yielded as one :class:`BlobRecord`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blobs:8 of
msgid ""
"**Multiple references**: the server returns a framed stream with one "
"frame per blob.  Each :class:`BlobRecord` carries the blob's MIME type "
"and custom file name (v3+) from the frame header."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.read_blobs:12 of
msgid ""
"References must be UTF-8 decodable strings or bytes.  Binary (non-UTF-8) "
"references returned for nested BLOB columns are not supported by the "
"generic ``BlobRead`` endpoint; reading them raises "
":class:`StorageClientError`.  Compression follows the tunnel pattern: "
"``compress_option`` (default ``None`` = uncompressed) or the shorthand "
"``compress_algo``.  Pass ``compress_algo=\"lz4\"`` / ``\"zstd\"`` to "
"request a compressed response. When ``stream=True``, returns a "
":class:`BlobStreamReader` for incremental file-like reads; otherwise "
"returns a :class:`BlobDataIterator` yielding :class:`BlobRecord`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_batch:1 of
msgid "Batch-upload multiple blobs in one request."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_batch:3 of
msgid ""
"Each :class:`BlobWriteItem` is framed and streamed to the server via "
"chunked transfer-encoding — the full batch body is never materialized.  "
"Compression via ``compress_option`` (default ``None`` = uncompressed).  "
"Returns :class:`WriteBlobResponse` with blob_references matching input "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_stream:1 of
msgid "Create a streaming writer for a single blob upload."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_stream:3 of
msgid ""
"Uses chunked transfer-encoding; compression via ``compress_option`` "
"(default ``None`` = uncompressed; ``ZSTD``/``LZ4_FRAME`` opt-in via "
"Content-Encoding).  The returned :class:`BlobStreamWriter` computes MD5 "
"incrementally and verifies on ``finish()``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_stream:8 of
msgid ""
"``column_name`` is the dot-path name (a key of "
":meth:`WriteSchema.find_all_blob_column_ids`), resolved to the server-"
"assigned column ID via the write schema.  When omitted, the sole top-"
"level pure-BLOB column is auto-selected (raises if the schema has "
"multiple BLOB columns or any nested BLOB column)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.blob.BlobManager.write_blob_stream:14 of
msgid ""
"``partition_spec`` accepts the same types as "
":class:`~odps.types.PartitionSpec` (str, dict, or PartitionSpec)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobRecord:1 of
msgid "A single downloaded blob yielded by :class:`BlobDataIterator`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobRecord:3 of
msgid ""
"``custom_file_name`` is only populated when the client targets API v3+; "
"it is ``None`` on v2 (the ``CustomFileName`` header is not parsed)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobDataIterator:1 of
msgid "Iterator yielding :class:`BlobRecord` per blob."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobDataIterator.read_data:1 of
msgid "Read up to *size* bytes of the current blob's data (for BlobStreamReader)."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobDataIterator.skip_remaining_data_and_footer:1
#: of
msgid "Skip *remaining_bytes* of unread data and the trailing footer."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobStreamReader:1 of
msgid "File-like reader for streaming blob data from a :class:`BlobDataIterator`."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobStreamReader:3 of
msgid ""
"Provides ``read(size)`` for incremental reads of the current blob, "
"``mime_type`` / ``custom_file_name`` properties, and a ``next()`` method "
"to advance to the next blob.  Avoids materializing entire blobs."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobStreamReader:7 of
msgid ""
"If ``next()`` is called before the current blob is fully read, the reader"
" **auto-drains** the remaining bytes.  Returns ``None`` from ``next()`` "
"when no more blobs remain."
msgstr ""
"If ``next()`` is called before the current blob is fully read, the reader"
" **auto-drains** the remaining bytes.  Returns ``None`` from ``next()`` "
"when no more blobs remain."

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_reader.BlobStreamReader.next:1 of
msgid "Advance to the next blob in-place. Returns ``self`` or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter:1 of
msgid "Stream writer for single blob upload with MD5 checksum verification."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter:3 of
msgid ""
"Wraps a :class:`RequestsIO` + compressor pipeline.  Data written via ``"
"write()`` is compressed (if requested) and streamed to the server in "
"chunks via chunked transfer-encoding — the full blob is never held in "
"memory.  MD5 is computed incrementally on the uncompressed data and "
"verified against the server response on ``finish()``."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter.finish:1 of
msgid "Finish writing, send the data, and verify MD5."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter.finish:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns the parsed :class:`WriteBlobResponse` on success. Raises "
":class:`odps.errors.ChecksumError` on MD5 mismatch, or "
":class:`MaxStorageError` if the upload fails with a non-200 response."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter.writable:1 of
msgid "Return whether object was opened for writing."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.io.blob_writer.BlobStreamWriter.writable:3 of
msgid "If False, write() will raise OSError."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.options.BlobWriteItem:1 of
msgid "A single blob item for batch upload."
msgstr ""

#: odps.maxstorage.options.BlobWriteItem:5 of
msgid ""
"Prefer :meth:`TableArrowWriter.build_blob_write_item` or :meth:`"
"BlobManager.build_blob_write_item` to construct items — they resolve ``"
"column_id``, normalize ``partition_spec``, and stamp ``api_version`` "
"automatically.  Constructing :class:`BlobWriteItem` directly requires "
"knowledge of server-assigned column IDs and wire-format details."
msgstr ""

